# Force LF line endings for all shell scripts (cross-platform)
*.sh text eol=lf
# Markdown and JSON are safe with LF too
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
# The JS entry point must be LF too. It is the npm `bin` target, so on
# macOS/Linux npm runs it through its shebang line — and a CRLF file leaves a
# stray carriage return after "node", which makes env fail with
# "No such file or directory". Missed by the v2.10.2 CRLF pass; caught 2026-07-30.
*.js text eol=lf
